<!--
    Cast campaign, the `(char *)<call>` residue.  kuna printed

        v1 = (char *)skip_blanks(a0);

    under its own `char * skip_blanks(char *a0)` declaration in the same
    listing: the callee's recovered return type never reached the call, so a
    caller that keeps the result as a `char *` converted it from a type the
    call does not have.  On coreutils tail -O0 the same shape is
    `sub_e8ca(4,(char *)sub_43ee(a0))` beside `char * sub_43ee(unsigned long *a0)`.

    Root cause (P4 output prototype).  Upstream's `TypeOpCall::getOutputLocal`
    answers only for a LOCKED output; a recovered callee's return type is never
    locked, so the call produces an unknown of its width, and ActionSetCasts
    casts it to whatever the caller keeps it as.

    THIS FIXTURE IS THE NEGATIVE CONTROL.  `option callrettype on` types a call's
    result with the return type its callee stated, and a callee states it only
    after its own decompile in a whole-binary `decompile-all`, which decompiles
    callees before callers (`protoorder`).  This harness decompiles ONE function
    from a byte image: `skip_blanks` states nothing when the console decompiles
    it, so the option must add nothing and both passes print `upper_of_rest`
    byte for byte alike.  (Here the call prints no cast in either pass: without
    `protoorder`'s argument types the caller keeps the result as the integer
    the call produces.)  The statement is recorded only where
    `park_recovered_proto` is true, which only
    decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/src/decompile_all.rs sets.

    The POSITIVE witness is the same code as a real program,
    decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/callrettype_gcc_O0_x86_64
    (source beside it), under `make test-cli`:
    tests/cli/callrettype-types-a-call-by-its-callees-return.json prints
    `v1 = skip_blanks(a0);` and tests/cli/callrettype-off-keeps-the-conversion.json
    is its option-off arm; kuna-cli/tests/decompile_all_cli.rs
    `a_call_result_typed_by_its_callee_round_trips_through_the_printed_c`
    compiles both arms and checks they compute what the binary computes.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "output-prototype".  Pass 1 pins `off`; pass 2 pins
    that `on` alone, with nothing stated, adds nothing.
-->
